**Re-check the PR range immediately before the refresh receipt POST.**

`refresh` checks the PR state and merge base at `src/policy/crq/receiptPrepare.ts:282-287`. It then makes further GitHub reads (`reviews` at line 288, `openMajor` at line 328) before publishing at line 352. The POST sends only `commit_id` (head) and no base binding. If the base changes during those reads, the PASS for head `H` is still published. It does not cover the new range. Repeat the open, head, and merge-base checks after the last read and before `postReview`. This narrows the race window to the request itself. It does not remove it, because the review API has no base binding.

